course: dictionary
lesson: 12968
title: Exempt: free from a rule
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: When something is exempt, it does not have to follow a rule, pay a charge or do a task that others must do. Look at the clue word «from»: exempt from means free from.
explain: «Children are exempt from the charge.» Other people must pay the charge, but children do not have to pay it. Exempt is an adjective here, because it describes the children.
explain: Exempt can also be a verb, which means to free someone from a rule or payment. «The doctor's note exempted Mia from PE.» The note set Mia free from PE, so she did not have to do it.
fact: Exempt means free from a rule, duty or payment that others must follow.
fact: As a verb, exempt means to free someone from a rule or payment.
fact: The phrase to remember is «exempt from», as in «exempt from the test».
fact: «Tax-exempt» means not charged tax.
fact: The verb changes its ending: exempt, exempts, exempted, exempting.
exercise: «Children are exempt from the charge.» What does exempt mean here? | Forced to pay twice | Angry about the bill | *Free from having to pay it | Given a prize for paying
exercise: «The doctor's note exempted Mia from PE.» What did the note do for Mia? | *Freed her from PE | Made her run extra laps | Gave her a new PE kit | Told her to sit down
exercise: Which word means free from a rule that others must follow? | Ancient | Barely | Glum | *Exempt
test: «Sam was exempt from the spelling test because he was ill.» What does exempt mean here? | Given extra spelling words | Late for the test | Top of the class in spelling | *Free from having to take the test
test: Yesterday the teacher ___ Ali from homework. Which word fits the gap? | exempt | exempting | *exempted | exempts
exam: In a maths problem, «exempt people are taken out before we work out the cost.» What does exempt mean here? | Counted twice in the total | Added to the cost | *Not counted, because they are free from the charge | Forgotten by the teacher
